# Regex literal unknown flag rejected

Verifies the `z` flag is rejected at compile time: no regex value is produced
and the diagnostic names the offending flag with its source span.

>>> source
const bad: regex = /abc/z
print(bad)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `/abc/z` for type `regex`: unknown flag `z` in regex literal at Span { start: 19, end: 25 }

<<< exit
1
